  "description": "SABQIY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C61 H86 Cu6 Dy3 N6 O30 3+,C1 H4 O1,N1 O3 1-,4(H2 O1),2(Br1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.063-3.867 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 79.72-114.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C62H98N7O38Br2Cu6Dy3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
